,"location":"Secretary of State","sequence":20,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Chaptered by Secretary of State - Chapter 80, Statutes of 2025.","time":null,"votes":[]}],"affectedStatutes":[{"action":"IS_ADDED","code":"ELEC","text":"Section 12263 is added to the Elections Code, to read:"}],"approvedDate":"2025-07-30","chapter":{"citation":"Chapter 80, Statutes of 2025","number":"80","type":"CHP","year":"2025"},"chapteredDate":"2025-07-30","committees":[],"conditions":[],"contentHash":"8f42b5485856b3f7d615fe14e2faaa89948b2fc38c595c8903c53ff90d4e0cd2","cosponsorCount":null,"digest":"Existing law requires the county elections official to divide the area under their jurisdiction into precincts and to prepare detailed maps or exterior descriptions of the precincts. If changes or alterations to precinct boundaries are made, existing law requires the elections official to prepare new maps or exterior descriptions. Existing law provides that precinct boundary changes occurring less than 125 days before an election are not effective for purposes of that election.\n\nThis bill would require the registrar of voters in each county to make available, upon request by any member of the public, a map in digital form provided free of charge that shows the effective boundaries of each precinct within the county.\n\nBy imposing new duties on local officials with respect to elections, the bill would create a state-mandated local program.\n\nThe California Constitution requires the state to reimburse local agencies and school districts for certain costs mandated by the state. Statutory provisions establish procedures for making that reimbursement.\n\nThis bill would provide that, if the Commission on State Mandates determines that the bill contains costs mandated by the state, reimbursement for those costs shall be made pursuant to the statutory provisions noted above.","digestDate":null,"digestVersion":null,"effective":{"basis":"not_verified","date":null,"note":"No effective date is recorded in the official bill data and DemocracyHQ has not verified one. A non-urgency statute enacted in a regular session generally takes effect on January 1 after a 90-day period (Cal. Const. art. IV, § 8(c)), but a bill may state other operative dates."},"expiryClauses":[],"firstObservedAt":"2026-11-20T01:12:59Z","id":"ca-20252026-ab17","identifier":"AB 17","indicators":{"Appropriation":"NO","BudgetBill":"NO","Election":"NO","FiscalCommittee":"YES","ImmediateEffect":"NO","LocalProgram":"YES","TaxLevy":"NO","Urgency":"NO","UsualCurrentExpenses":"NO","VoteRequired":"MAJORITY"},"introducedDate":"2024-12-02","issueTags":[{"matchCount":null,"matchedField":"official subject line","matchedText":"Elections: precinct maps.","ruleId":"tag-admin-2","tag":"election-administration"}],"judicialNote":"Legislative status does not show whether a court has blocked, narrowed or upheld any provision. Check the linked litigation, which may be incomplete.","lastActionDate":"2025-07-30","lastActionText":"Chaptered by Secretary of State - Chapter 80, Statutes of 2025.","lastCheckedAt":"2026-11-21T12:46:07Z","leadAuthors":"Introduced by Assembly Member Alanis","legislativeStatus":{"currentHouse":"Secretary of State","currentLocation":null,"currentStatus":"Chaptered","measureState":"Chaptered"},"legislativeSubjects":[],"measureType":"Assembly Bill","officialUrl":"https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/billNavClient.xhtml?bill_id=202520260AB17","policyArea":null,"relatedMeasures":[],"selection":{"matchedField":"official subject line (latest version)","matchedText":"Elections","ruleId":"ca-select-2"},"session":"2025-2026 Regular Session","shortTitles":[],"sourceId":"ca-leginfo-bulk","sourcePublishedAt":"2026-11-16T05:26:36Z","sourceRecordUrl":null,"sponsors":[],"state":"06","stateAbbr":"CA","subject":"Elections: precinct maps.","title":"An act to add Section 12263 to the Elections Code, relating to elections.","verification":{"checkedAt":"2026-11-21T12:46:07Z","me